id: drunk
name: Drunk
kind: state
levels: 2
# A Special State (the user's terminology): no Narrative Requirement - only an effect that gives it enters it (the Sake
# Bottle's Drink).
specialState: true
description: >
  Tipsy: Saving Throws and Combat Rolls L(T) lower, the Natural Result of Strike and Dodge L higher. Plastered: the
  Combat Conditions do nothing (but Pinned, Suffocating, Stress Exhaustion and Transfigured).
text: >
  Tipsy (Level 1)
  (1)-[Passive]: Reduce your Saving Throws and Combat Rolls by L(T).
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase the Natural Result of your Strike and Dodge Rolls by L.

  Plastered (Level 2)
  (1)-[Passive]: Ignore the effects of all Combat Conditions (except Pinned, Suffocating, Stress Exhaustion, and
  Transfigured).

---

# Everything accumulates upwards, as Raging's does: at Level 2 Tipsy's is still running, at L 2.
# Plastered is read where the Combat Conditions' effects are gathered (effects/registry.mjs conditionPrograms): every
# Combat Condition's script left out but those four. What code reads of a Condition outside its script is not touched.

[passive from 1]
save.all -= L(T);
combatRolls -= L(T);
strike.natural += L;
dodge.natural += L;
